# if3310-tubes backend ("if3310-api", internal only — reached via
# labs/if3310-tubes's nginx proxy at /api/, /store/, and /ws) — Express REST
# API on :3000 plus a separate raw ws.Server on :8000.
# Build context MUST be the repo root:
#   docker build -t egolab-if3310-api:latest -f labs/if3310-tubes/Dockerfile.api .
FROM node:20-bookworm
WORKDIR /app
COPY projects/if3310-tubes/backend/package.json projects/if3310-tubes/backend/package-lock.json* ./
RUN npm ci
COPY projects/if3310-tubes/backend/ ./
# Fixes on top of the upstream checkout — see labs/if3310-tubes/overrides
# (hardcoded frontend URLs in CORS config and push-notification payloads;
# see the comment at the top of overrides/backend/src/index.ts).
COPY labs/if3310-tubes/overrides/backend/ ./
# Dead code: a raw pg.Pool with hardcoded (and wrong — "postgresql" isn't
# the real db/user/password) credentials, never imported by anything —
# the app's real Prisma-backed subscription handling lives in
# controllers/notifController.ts. Remove rather than leave it as a trap for
# a future edit that re-enables it.
RUN rm -f src/models/subscriptionModel.ts
RUN npx prisma generate

EXPOSE 3000 8000
CMD ["npx", "tsx", "src/index.ts"]
